  "_note": "RUN 6 -- SETTLES THE 300 ms COMB. ANTENNA FITTED, -24 dBm.\n\nRun 4 (3360 keys, adv 200-1400 in 100 ms steps x broadcasts {4,6}) found delivery\ncollapses at every adv that is a multiple of 300: 69.3% vs 92.7%, p = 0.00005,\nat the same adv in both broadcast arms. That rules out dwell. The leading model is\nphase locking against a duty-cycled scanner with scan interval S: an advertiser\nvisits S/gcd(adv,S) distinct phases, and adv = k*S visits exactly one, so a phase\nin the scanner's dead time is never escaped. S = 300 ms fits all 13 levels.\n\nThis run attacks the two things run 4 could not settle.\n\nARM A -- off-grid adv {150, 250, 350, 450} at broadcasts {4, 6}.\nRun 4's 100 ms grid forced gcd(adv,300) to be 100 or 300, so it could only\ndistinguish 1 phase from 3 and could not show a GRADIENT. Predictions if S = 300:\n  adv 250, 350 -> gcd  50 -> 6 phases -> cleanest cells in the matrix\n  adv 150      -> gcd 150 -> 2 phases -> INTERMEDIATE, between locked and clean\n  adv 450      -> gcd 150 -> 2 phases -> intermediate\nadv 450 is also the discriminator against S = 150: under S = 150 it is a multiple\nof the scan interval and should be FULLY locked (severe), not intermediate. One\nlevel separates the two candidate scan intervals.\n\nARM B -- escape curve. adv 600 (locked) against adv 500 (clean control), each at\nbroadcasts {4, 8, 16}. This is the most consequential comparison in the run.\nThe spec's 0-10 ms random advDelay per advertising event gives phase a slow random\nwalk, so more events = more chances to escape a dead phase; run 4 already shows 6\nbroadcasts beating 4 at exactly the penalised levels and nowhere else. If that\nmechanism is real the penalty at adv 600 should largely VANISH by 16 broadcasts,\nand the rule becomes 'avoid multiples of 300 ms below ~8 broadcasts per key'.\nIf the penalty PERSISTS at 16 broadcasts, advDelay is not doing its job on this\ncontroller and the finding is a property of THIS TRANSMITTER rather than of the\nrelay network -- which is currently the largest open question in the report.\nRun 2 gives the ceiling for arm B: at -24 dBm, 16 broadcasts delivered 100%, so\nany shortfall at adv 600 / bc 16 is the comb and nothing else. Run 4 supplies the\nbc 4 point at adv 600 (59.2%) and 500 (92.5%); both are replicated here in-run.\n\nDESIGN. 14 conditions x 9 reps + 12 anchors. Condition order rotates by stride 5\nper block (coprime with 14, so every condition visits every slot). Anchors open\nevery block and bisect blocks 2, 5 and 8.\n\nANALYSIS. Group by (adv, broadcasts). Arm A: test for a graded response ordered\nby phases-visited = 300/gcd(adv,300), not a binary one. Arm B: test the adv 600\nvs adv 500 gap at each broadcast count -- the prediction is that the gap shrinks\nmonotonically and is near zero at 16.\n\nRESWEEP AT LEAST 2 h AFTER TRANSMIT ENDS. Run 4's first sweep ran ~1 min after\nthe last cell and read 29.6% for that final hour against 76.1% on re-sweep.",
